function publish scanner changes in {string:root} using {a pointer to github tools:tools}:
    execute:
        set arguments to an empty list of string
        append the string form of "add" to arguments
        append the string form of "-A" to arguments
        set staged to run git using tools with arguments in root
        free arguments
        if the inverse of staged's succeeded:
            return a failed github publication reporting staged's error message

        set arguments to an empty list of string
        append the string form of "diff" to arguments
        append the string form of "--cached" to arguments
        append the string form of "--quiet" to arguments
        set difference to run git using tools with arguments in root
        free arguments
        if difference's succeeded:
            return a successful github publication changed false
        if the inverse of difference's launched or difference's exit code != (1 as a word sized integer):
            return a failed github publication reporting difference's error message

        set arguments to an empty list of string
        append the string form of "-c" to arguments
        append the string form of "user.name=OpenAEC Convention Enforcer" to arguments
        append the string form of "-c" to arguments
        append the string form of "user.email=41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com" to arguments
        append the string form of "commit" to arguments
        append the string form of "-m" to arguments
        append the string form of "Apply repository convention fixes" to arguments
        set committed to run git using tools with arguments in root
        free arguments
        if the inverse of committed's succeeded:
            return a failed github publication reporting committed's error message

        set arguments to an empty list of string
        append the string form of "push" to arguments
        append the string form of "--force-with-lease" to arguments
        append the string form of "origin" to arguments
        append the scanner branch name to arguments
        set pushed to run git using tools with arguments in root
        free arguments
        if the inverse of pushed's succeeded:
            return a failed github publication reporting pushed's error message
        return a successful github publication changed true

